# Project: YorùbáOCR Research

## What this project is
A benchmark dataset + fine-tuning study for Yorùbá OCR submitted to
Deep Learning Indaba 2026 (IJCAI volume). The active comparison contains
PaddleOCR PP-OCRv3 English pretrained recognition, PaddleOCR-VL-1.6 and
GLM-OCR zero-shot baselines, and PaddleOCR-VL-1.6 supervised adaptation.
Classical PaddleOCR recognition fine-tuning is optional. The researcher built a custom annotation platform
(yoruba-ocr.vercel.app) and exported data in PaddleOCR line-crop format.

## Verified dataset facts (do not invent alternatives)
- Source: Yorùbá di Wúrà Book Series (printed books, 2021)
- Language: Standard Yorùbá, corrected=yes for all entries
- Format: line crops (PNG) + tab-separated label files (PaddleOCR format)
  - Each label line: images/{split}/hash_lineNNNN.png<TAB>ground_truth_text
- 25+ independent annotation export batches in data/raw/
- Frozen split: 2,945 unique lines (2,367 train / 252 validation / 326 test)
- Character dictionary: built from consolidated labels (currently **99** graphemes excl. space on disk; varies with hygiene)
- Metadata columns: image, text, source, year, dialect, corrected, parent_image, line_index
- Consolidated data lives in data/processed/ after running consolidate_data.py

## Pipeline scripts (in execution order)
1. scripts/consolidate_data.py  — merge exports, deduplicate, copy to data/processed/
2. scripts/analyze_dataset.py   — EDA: char/diacritic distribution, text length stats
3. scripts/generate_paddleocr_config.py   — download pretrained weights + write fine-tune YAML
4. scripts/train_paddleocr_recognition.py — optional classical recognition fine-tuning
5. scripts/evaluate_paddleocr_en_pretrained.py — English pretrained PP-OCRv3 control
6. scripts/eval_paddleocrvl16.py — PaddleOCR-VL-1.6 zero-shot or SFT-checkpoint evaluation
7. scripts/eval_glm_ocr.py — GLM-OCR zero-shot evaluation
8. scripts/export_paddleocrvl16_sft.py and scripts/train_paddleocrvl16_sft.py — supervised adaptation
9. scripts/analyze_stratified_errors.py, scripts/ablate_der_universe.py, scripts/bootstrap_metric_cis.py — robustness analyses
10. scripts/compile_results.py and scripts/generate_plots.py — paper tables and figures
11. scripts/metrics_lifecycle.py and scripts/refresh_dataset_report.py — run hygiene
12. scripts/publish_hf_dataset.py — optional dataset release

## Models being compared
1. PaddleOCR PP-OCRv3 English pretrained — classical zero-shot control
2. PaddleOCR-VL-1.6 — zero-shot multimodal OCR baseline
3. GLM-OCR — zero-shot multimodal OCR baseline
4. PaddleOCR-VL-1.6 SFT — supervised adaptation; `lm_head` is the default scope
5. PaddleOCR recognition fine-tune — optional classical comparison

## Metrics
- CER — Character Error Rate (NFC-normalised edit distance / gt char count)
- WER — Word Error Rate (NFC-normalised word-level edit distance / gt word count)
- DER — Diacritic Error Rate (novel contribution):
    pred_diacs = [c for c in NFD(pred) if unicodedata.combining(c)]
    gt_diacs   = [c for c in NFD(gt)   if unicodedata.combining(c)]
    DER = edit_distance(pred_diacs, gt_diacs) / len(gt_diacs)
  Measures tone mark and subdot fidelity specifically — the key failure mode
  of English pretrained models on Yorùbá text.

## All results must be traceable
- Every number in the paper must map to an entry in results/tables/metrics.csv
- Per-sample JSONL logs are written alongside every eval run
- Never write a metric value in prose that is not in results/tables/

## Terminology: always use these exact forms
- Yorùbá (with diacritics, never "Yoruba")
- diacritic minimal pairs (not "similar characters")
- toneme, tonograph, combining diacritic
- low-resource (hyphenated when modifier)
- fine-tuning (hyphenated)
- CER, WER, DER (always capitalised)

